# DraggableArea

`DraggableArea` is another name for [`DraggableElement`](/docs/components/DraggableElement): the package exports the same component under both names, as react-advanced-cropper does. The stencils use the `DraggableArea` name for the part you grab to move the stencil, and the default `activationDistance` of 30 pixels suits that role on touch screens.

```
StencilWrapper
└─ BoundingBox
   └─ DraggableArea            (moves the stencil)
      └─ StencilOverlay
         └─ preview
```

## Usage

In a [custom stencil](/docs/tutorials/custom-stencil), forward its moves to the cropper:

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import { DraggableArea, type CropperRef } from 'svelte-advanced-cropper';

	interface Props {
		cropper: CropperRef;
		movable?: boolean;
	}

	let { cropper, movable = true }: Props = $props();
</script>

<DraggableArea
	disabled={!movable}
	onMove={(directions) => cropper.moveCoordinates(directions)}
	onMoveEnd={() => cropper.moveCoordinatesEnd()}
	class="my-stencil__draggable-area"
>
	<div class="my-stencil__preview"></div>
</DraggableArea>
```

`moveCoordinates` expects on-screen pixels, which is exactly what `onMove` reports.

## Props

The props, the event handling and the CSS class (`advanced-cropper-draggable-element`) are those of [`DraggableElement`](/docs/components/DraggableElement#props). The built-in stencils add `advanced-cropper-rectangle-stencil__draggable-area` (or the `circle-stencil` equivalent) and their `draggableAreaClassName` prop.
